# Input rate control

Choose the mechanism by intent — do not sprinkle `setTimeout` as a default.

| Intent | Mechanism |
| ------ | --------- |
| Wait until they stop typing, then fetch | Trailing debounce |
| Act on the first tap, then coalesce a burst | Leading-plus-trailing throttle |
| Finger is dragging a value the UI can only show coarsely | Quantize to the smallest visible unit and dedupe |
| A write must not double-fire | In-flight guard in the handler (not only a `disabled` prop) |
| Local list filter already in memory | Nothing — stay responsive |

## Continuous gesture / drag

- Never debounce something a finger is dragging — the visual must track the finger. Quantize to the
  smallest unit the label or slot can show, dedupe, and keep the paint on the UI thread.
- RNGH `Gesture.*` objects must be `useMemo`'d. Rebuilding a `Gesture` on every React render
  re-attaches the recognizer mid-gesture and causes scrubber / drag thrash.
- Gate worklet-to-JS hops (`runOnJS`) on a **changed quantized value**, not every frame.
- Per-frame `setState` during drag must compare against the previous value first (e.g.
  `isSameHoverTarget`) so an unchanged slot does not re-render the tree.

## Taps that write

- Every tap that writes to the network or durable storage needs an in-flight guard inside the
  handler. A `disabled` prop alone is not enough (programmatic calls, accessibility actions).
- Prefer a shared helper (`createInFlightGuard`) keyed by action + resource id when many call sites
  share one mutation hook.

## Concurrent async reads

- Concurrent fetches that apply to the same UI need a request-generation id (see
  `feedRequestIdRef` on Home, `searchRequestIdRef` on Search) so a slow response cannot overwrite a
  newer one.

## Reuse before inventing

- Prefer an existing coalescing window before adding a new timer: playback outbox intervals
  (`PLAYBACK_POSITION_NETWORK_INTERVAL_MS`, `PLAYBACK_POSITION_LOCAL_INTERVAL_MS`,
  `PLAYBACK_SEEK_NETWORK_COALESCE_MS`), download store ~2 Hz channel.
- Precedents: Search `SEARCH_DEBOUNCE_MS` 450, web `SearchInput` / `useTableFilterState`.

## Do not

- Debounce a local in-memory list filter (`ListFilterField`).
- Debounce the visible playback clock — clocks already quantize to whole seconds.
- Persist free-text filter terms to device prefs (see **filter-sort-persistence**).
